# Paperia Theme

Custom theme slug/name: `paperia`.

Follow **Learning Mode** (`paperia-learning`): explain each step and list WordPress Admin actions whenever the dashboard is involved.

## Location

Develop the theme at:

`wordpress/wp-content/themes/paperia/`

Do not edit default themes (Twenty*). Do not put theme logic in plugins unless it must be site-wide infrastructure.

## Architecture

Keep files small and focused. Prefer WordPress APIs over custom code.

```
paperia/
├── style.css                 # Theme header only (compiled CSS is enqueued separately)
├── functions.php             # Bootstrap only; require includes
├── index.php
├── header.php
├── footer.php
├── front-page.php
├── single.php
├── page.php
├── archive.php
├── 404.php
├── search.php
├── template-parts/           # Reusable sections only
│   ├── header/
│   ├── footer/
│   ├── content/
│   └── components/
├── inc/                      # PHP modules (setup, assets, ACF, helpers)
├── assets/
│   ├── scss/                 # Source styles (never edit compiled CSS by hand)
│   ├── css/                  # Compiled output
│   ├── js/
│   └── images/
└── acf-json/                 # ACF Local JSON (versioned)
```

## Reuse rules

- Never place large HTML blocks inside page templates.
- Extract reusable UI into `template-parts/` and load with `get_template_part()`.
- Every template-part has one job (e.g. site header, card, hero).
- Share markup via template-parts; share logic via `inc/` helpers.
- Prefer CSS and WordPress APIs before custom JavaScript for UI chrome and forms.
- **Exception — motion:** intentional GSAP / ScrollTrigger / parallax JS is required (see `paperia-animation`). Do not leave marketing pages static.

## Customization

Theme options and custom fields use **ACF** (not hardcoding). Colors, typography, header/footer content, and page-specific fields come from ACF Options or field groups.
